PR sketch: lightweight session labels spike

Summary
- Adds a minimal live-session label layer to zmx.
- Labels are key=value string pairs attached to the running session daemon.
- Intended for humans and tools/agents to identify and select sessions.
- Naming follows Kubernetes label conventions.

What this spike adds
- IPC tags: LabelGet, LabelSet, LabelUnset, LabelClear, LabelData
- CLI: zmx label get/set/unset/clear [session] [k=v...]
- zmx list --labels (now default), --no-labels, --where key=value, --where key~=pattern
- Built-in fields (name, start_dir, cmd) queryable via --where without setting labels
- Shell completions for bash, zsh, fish, nu
- Efficient label fetching: Info + LabelGet batched on same socket connection
- Friendly error messages for old daemons, missing sessions, missing ZMX_SESSION

GitHub issue: https://github.com/neurosnap/zmx/issues/183
